From: HobbyOS H3-winefix
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Block SIGQUIT once a thread has started to exit.

wineserver's kill_thread() SIGQUITs every thread still on the process list
when it terminates a process.  A thread that exits on its own
(NtTerminateThread(self) -> exit_thread()) stays listed until the server
processes its request-fd hangup, and exit_thread()/abort_thread() block only
server_block_set, which has no SIGQUIT.  The signal can then land:
 - after glibc's pthread_exit() cleared the teb_key TSD slot:
   quit_handler() -> is_inside_syscall() -> NtCurrentTeb() == NULL
   -> read of NULL+0x3a8 (ntdll_thread_data.kernel_stack) -> SIGSEGV;
 - earlier in the exit: abort_thread() runs a second time, decrementing
   nb_threads twice and closing the server fds twice.
Seen on HobbyOS as "services.exe memory fault VA=0x3A8 PC=quit_handler+0x40"
in ~0.7 % of Wine boots (docs/cp-winefix.md).

Applies to wine-11.0 (dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c).  Build: CP_WINE_PATCHES=
tools/cp/wine-patches bash tools/cp/build-wine.sh all.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
@@ -1469,11 +1469,32 @@
 
 
 /***********************************************************************
+ *           block_exit_signals
+ *
+ * Block the server signals and SIGQUIT for a thread that has started to exit.
+ * The server sends SIGQUIT to every thread still on the process list when it
+ * terminates the process (or the thread), and a thread that is exiting on its
+ * own stays on that list until the server notices its request fd was closed.
+ * A SIGQUIT in that window re-enters abort_thread() (nb_threads is decremented
+ * twice and the server fds are closed twice), or, once glibc has cleared the
+ * teb_key slot in pthread_exit(), faults in quit_handler() on NtCurrentTeb()
+ * returning NULL.  The thread is exiting anyway, so the signal can wait.
+ */
+static void block_exit_signals(void)
+{
+    sigset_t set = server_block_set;
+
+    sigaddset( &set, SIGQUIT );
+    pthread_sigmask( SIG_BLOCK, &set, NULL );
+}
+
+
+/***********************************************************************
  *           abort_thread
  */
 void abort_thread( int status )
 {
-    pthread_sigmask( SIG_BLOCK, &server_block_set, NULL );
+    block_exit_signals();
     if (InterlockedDecrement( &nb_threads ) <= 0) abort_process( status );
     pthread_exit_wrapper( status );
 }
@@ -1496,7 +1517,7 @@
     static void *prev_teb;
     TEB *teb;
 
-    pthread_sigmask( SIG_BLOCK, &server_block_set, NULL );
+    block_exit_signals();
 
     if (InterlockedDecrement( &nb_threads ) <= 0) exit_process( status );
 
